# Reviewing changes in `components/`

The unified reviewer (`prompts/codeReviewer/v3/`) loads **`components/REVIEW.md`** for
any changed path under `components/`. That map cites rule IDs from
`components/AGENTS.md` (e.g. `Invariant #3`, `V2`, `TAP-3`) — it never restates the rule
text.

Deterministic checks that fire here first (precedence over LLM):
- D1 dependency table (`check_dependency_rules`) — components must not import `langgraph`/
  `langchain`; no peer imports (`router.py` must not import `evaluator.py`).
- D5 anti-patterns (`detect_anti_patterns` AP-2 peer coupling / AP-5 / AP-6).
- D1 test-import rule — `tests/components/` must not import orchestration.

Dispatch the reviewer:

```bash
python -m meta.code_reviewer --from-git-diff --git-base HEAD --prompt-version v3 --output review.json
```

Deterministic findings are the gate; the v3 LLM judge is WI-8 certified (TPR/TNR = 1.0) so LLM verdicts are gate-grade for the routed LLM-only rules — re-record when the judge model changes.
Full contract: `docs/skills/code-review/SKILL.md`.
